<title>USA: Volvo GM to shut Ohio truck plant.</title>
<headline>Volvo GM to shut Ohio truck plant.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, N.C. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volvo GM Heavy Truck Corp said Thursday it would close its Orrville, Ohio, truck plant next April and consolidate assembly operations at its Dublin, Va., facility.</p>
<p>The company said it would offer jobs at other locations to some of the 473 employees of the Ohio plant. It did not specify how many of them would receive job offers.  </p>
<p>The consolidation in Virginia would make industrial operations more efficient and lower manufacturing costs, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Truck models produced in Orrville include the Xpeditor, Autocar, WG straight truck, Autohauler and the FE series.</p>
<p>Normal production is expected to continue at the plant through April. It currently produces 15 trucks a day.</p>
</text>
